---
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import LibraryHero from '../../components/LibraryHero.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Library hero" padding="none" code={'<div class="family-dotnet">\n  <LibraryHero title="…" highlight="…" highlightClass="text-pair from-violet to-blue" lead="…">\n    <Button slot="actions" … />\n  </LibraryHero>\n</div>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The opening of a library, product, Aero or Contact page: a two-line display headline over a bloom in the family's colours (set by the <code>.family-&lt;id&gt;</code> wrapper), a standfirst and the actions. The second line takes the family's gradient pair, or the whole brand gradient with <code>spectrum</code>.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="family-dotnet">
        <LibraryHero title="Products for .NET" highlight="Built for Precision" highlightClass="text-pair from-violet to-blue" lead="A suite of general-purpose, production-ready libraries for modern .NET, with a strong emphasis on correctness, composability and value semantics.">
            <Button slot="actions" href="#library-hero" variant="primary" size="large">Browse on NuGet</Button>
        </LibraryHero>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Spectrum hero" padding="none" code={'<LibraryHero title="…" highlight="…" spectrum lead="…">…</LibraryHero>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The same hero blooming in the whole brand spectrum, as on Aero and Contact. The home page's Studio hero and the AI page's circuit hero are one-offs: <code>StudioHero</code> and <code>AiCircuitSection</code>.</p></Fragment>
    <LibraryHero title="Start the conversation" highlight="We'll take it from there" spectrum lead="Whether you're exploring our products, thinking about consulting, or just want to talk through an idea, we'd be glad to help.">
        <Fragment slot="actions">
            <Button href="#spectrum-hero" variant="primary" size="large">Send a message</Button>
            <Button href="#spectrum-hero" variant="ghost" size="large" trailingIcon="arrow-right-bold">Book a meeting</Button>
        </Fragment>
    </LibraryHero>
</Specimen>
